  "case_id": "CASE-030",
  "category": "cvrp_adaptive_destroy_repair",
  "description": [
    "**CVRP adaptive large-neighborhood search with independent operator weights.** Use a symmetric matrix, a single depot and hard vehicle capacity. Begin from savings routes. At each iteration sample a destroy and a repair index independently.\n\n",
    "Destroy by uniform or related customer removal. Repair by greedy capacity-aware insertion or Regret-2 followed by completion of unassigned customers. Accept feasible full candidates using simulated annealing, while maintaining separate best and current route sets.\n\n",
    "Assign outcome rewards to both selected indices and update their two weight vectors each four attempts. Cooling shares those boundaries. The PDPTW source is adapted to one-node CVRP customers, with no CP-SAT route-refinement stage."
  ],
